      {
        "text": "Kam Buckner, a Democratic State Representative for Chicago's 26th District since 2019, is Speaker Pro Tempore. He was a vice president at Outfront Media and executive director of World Sport Chicago, a youth development nonprofit.",
        "cites": [1],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Kam Buckner, a Democratic State Representative for Chicago's 26th District since 2019, is Speaker Pro Tempore.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He was a vice president at Outfront Media and executive director of World Sport Chicago, a youth development nonprofit.",
            "cites": [1]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In 2026, laws he backed regulating consumer fees and expanding opportunities for people with records became law. A criminal justice reform bill he sponsored was signed in 2025. He sponsored gun control and collegiate athlete compensation legislation, and helped negotiate the state's clean energy package. He co-sponsored a bill requiring companies to disclose algorithmic pricing and let consumers opt out. He chiefly sponsored a megaprojects bill to convince the Chicago Bears to build an Arlington Heights stadium. He is a top House budget negotiator.",
        "cites": [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 1]
      }
    ]
  },
